{
  "results": [
    {
      "n": "G1",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–5 show the 3D scene rendering properly in Chrome with no blank screen or errors.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "G2",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 2–5 demonstrate camera orbiting and zooming around the bird, and OrbitControls in the code sets maxPolarAngle = Math.PI * 0.492 and maxDistance = 26 to keep the camera above the water and inside the sky dome.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "G3",
      "evidence": "The scene uses low-poly procedural tubes/cones, a single 1024x1024 planar water reflection, and one 2048x2048 shadow map with no post-processing, which will easily run above 30 fps on an integrated laptop GPU.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "1",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–5 display an on-screen text pill UI at the bottom reading 'Drag to Orbit 3D • Scroll to Zoom • Right-Drag to Pan', and panning/zooming are enabled alongside orbiting.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "2",
      "evidence": "In the animate() loop, water.material.uniforms['time'].value, flamingo.position.y, and footRipple.scale update continuously from page load without user input.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "3",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 shows a side-profile view at the flamingo's height with the bird centered and filling most of the vertical frame, matching the reference photo's framing.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "4",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 depicts a single flamingo standing in calm water in the same mid-stride pose as the photo, with one vertical supporting leg and one bent leg.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "5",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 matches the reference colour palette with a coral-orange neck and upper wing, paler salmon-pink body, pink legs, black flight feathers, and a pale cream facial/basal bill region leading to an orange mid-bill and black tip.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "6",
      "evidence": "Unlike the soft, seamless even blue of the reference photo, Screenshots 1–3 and 5 show a stark, high-contrast horizon line separating a dark blue sky from a much lighter blue water plane.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "7",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 3 show bright illumination on the front and right surfaces of the neck and chest, matching sunLight positioned at (7.5, 6.5, 5.5) in the front-right.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "8",
      "evidence": "In Screenshot 1, the neck forms a clear S-curve with the head bent over at the top and the hooked beak pointing downward.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "9",
      "evidence": "While the legs are long and thin with backward-bending joints, Screenshot 1 shows the neck base jutting below the chest as a thick disconnected cylinder, Screenshot 4 shows eyes protruding from the sides of the head, and the feet are simple red cones (ConeGeometry) rather than webbed feet.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "10",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1–3, the wings sit as smooth lobes against the sides of the body with narrow black cones sticking out the back, lacking the partly raised wing posture and exposed fan of black flight feathers seen in the photo.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "11",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1–3, only the left leg has a flat translucent disc around it while the right leg enters the water with no ripple ring at all, and the left foot sticks up as a small red spike.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "12",
      "evidence": "Although the water extends to the horizon without a visible edge, buildOrganicTube uses uncapped TubeGeometry (closed = false), leaving an open truncated cylinder visible where the bottom of the neck protrudes beneath the chest in Screenshot 1.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "13",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–3 show smooth directional shading across the rounded body and neck, transitioning from a bright lit front-right side to a softer shaded back-left side.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "14",
      "evidence": "In Screenshot 1, hemisphere fill lighting and ACES filmic tone mapping prevent any region from clipping to pure black or blowing out to pure white.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "15",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 has a crisp, hard horizon line dividing dark sky from light water instead of the smooth, soft out-of-focus gradient seen in the reference photo.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "16",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1–4, the body, neck, and wings look like smooth plastic tubes and ellipsoids with rigid cone spikes for flight feathers rather than soft, layered plumage.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "17",
      "evidence": "Although the leg joints are darker red-pink spheres, legMat uses clearcoat (0.25) and the beak tip shares plumageMat (roughness 0.58 with featherBump) so it appears matte rather than glossy black in Screenshot 1.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "18",
      "evidence": "Comparing Screenshot 4 (looking straight down) with Screenshots 1 and 5 (grazing angles) shows the Three.js Water shader reflecting much more strongly toward grazing angles.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "19",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 shows the pink legs reflecting vertically in the water as in the photo, and Screenshot 5 shows the full flamingo and legs reflected on the water surface.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "20",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–3 and 5 show a completely flat, horizontal water surface with no unintended tilt.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "21",
      "evidence": "In the code, footRipple is just a single MeshBasicMaterial ring on one leg pulsing in scale by 6%, so ripples neither spread outward across the water nor distort the Water shader's reflection.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "22",
      "evidence": "In animate(), subtle sine-wave motions are applied to flamingo.position.y and neckMesh.rotation.z to simulate gentle breathing and slight neck movement.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "23",
      "evidence": "In animate(), water.material.uniforms['time'].value advances at elapsed * 0.22, moving small wavelets continuously across the water normal map.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "24",
      "evidence": "All motions in animate() are driven by continuous low-frequency sine functions and seamless wrapped UV scrolling at slow real-world speeds without resets or jumps.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "25",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–3 and 5 reveal an obvious repeating horizontal tile pattern across the water normal map, and there is only a single flat ring mesh on one foot rather than concentric rings fading with distance.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "26",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–3 show the legs meeting the underside of the torso cleanly via feathered thigh cones and entering the water without unintended geometry clipping.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "27",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–4 show smooth vertex-colored surfaces on the bird with no visible UV texture seams or repeating texture patterns on the plumage.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "28",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–5 show clean antialiased 3D silhouettes against the sky and water with no jagged alpha cut-outs or halos.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "29",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 clearly reads as a simplified geometric 3D model with a disjointed tubular neck, spiky cone feathers, a stark horizon line, and an on-screen UI pill, so it could not pass for the reference photo at first glance.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "30",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 shows a soft shadow tucked directly beneath the coral wing covert on the flank and smooth shading along the shaded side of the neck consistent with the front-right sunLight.",
      "pass": true
    }
  ]
}
